Subject: [PATCH 01010/11171] [outer-loop] Diagnose verifier anti-ranking:
 brittle max() + 2 anti-families

Per operator directive (diagnose before building). On TRM's REAL candidate pool:

PER-FAMILY discrimination AUROC (>0.5 = ranks gold better):
  color_mapping 0.71, object_count 0.67, content_overlap 0.67, tiling 0.91 -> REAL signal
  v1 0.42, delta_pattern 0.43 -> ANTI-discriminative (prefer wrong candidates)
  palette_histogram 0.56 (weak), symmetry n/a (0 tasks)

AGGREGATION pass@2 (vote=0.452):
  union_max 0.194, mean 0.161, median 0.226  <- max() takes each candidate's WORST
    family, so any family mis-firing on gold sinks it -> catastrophic
  min_defined 0.419 (~vote), v1_only 0.387
  every leave-one-out still ~0.19 (TWO anti-families, not one)

VERDICT: NOT signal-absence -- it is the brittle max() aggregation + v1/delta_pattern
anti-discrimination. 4 families carry real but low-coverage signal. No simple
re-aggregation BEATS vote yet (best min=0.419<0.452). Next: a LEARNED combiner
(logistic group-CV, down-weighting v1/delta_pattern) is the definitive hand-feature
ceiling on TRM's pool; if it can't beat vote, GAP-3 learned/model-native energy is
confirmed as the only path.

